       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. At that dose the patient could develop severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. Overdoses of this size can also cause shock and non-cardiogenic pulmonary edema.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo. Here are some options:\n\n- **5 mg once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **10 mg once daily.** This is the maximum dose.\n\nTell me which dose you want and I'll enter it right away. If you meant 50 mg on purpose, the order will need to go through your pharmacy or the prescriber of record, because I can't enter a dose above the labeled maximum."
